<title>PERU: Lima bolsa changes list of blue-chip stocks.</title>
<headline>Lima bolsa changes list of blue-chip stocks.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Lima Stock Exchange began using Wednesday a new list of 15 blue-chip shares for its Selective Index, substituting three stocks with three other more heavily-traded issues.</p>
<p>The new list added electricity companies Edegel, Luz del Sur and metal manufacturer Fabrica de Aluminios y Metales del Peru.</p>
<p>They replaced brewery Compania Cervecera del Sur, telecom Tele 2000 and miner Buenaventura.</p>
<p>As well as the three additional stocks, the new list of blue-chips also keeps Telefonica B, Backus y Johnston, Compania Nacional de Cerveza, Banco de Credito, Edelnor, Holding Credicorp, Atacocha, Morococha, Southern Peru Limited, Minsur, D'Onofrio and Cementos Lima.</p>
<p>((-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
